  "implementation": [
    "native/image/windows_integrated.py selects the workspace base at initial staging, then composes its real PAM/runtime closure, the pinned completion/model closure, and one package with both opt-in flags. Fresh destinations are exclusive; failed or previous builds are not overwritten",
    "Both closed descriptors and every runtime/model member join the same publisher-required file inventory. Schema3 identity, nobody default UID65534 and WSL flags0 remain unchanged; creating the separately authenticated UID/GID1000 account does not change the default worker identity",
    "The inference runtime traversal now starts with the actual compiled platform worker as well as the private CPU completion runtime. Worker-only dependencies, including libsystemd.so.0, belong to both exact runtime manifests rather than only generic package RequiredFiles",
    "The production Windows inspector validates both descriptors under the closed workspace identity before reporting inference presence. The post-validation summary now reports the actual combined composition rather than treating schema3 as workspace-only",
    "The Windows manual console remains model-disabled unless a separate explicit inference operation is requested. The package does not turn health, PAM history, a Read receipt or package inspection into a product grant or Export authority",
    "Later native Life or other native-image development is not retroactively attributed to this retained profile-W package. Hyper-V remains owner-deferred and GWIN1/GWIN2 are not claimed complete by this record",
    "The 2026-10-31 refresh recompiles the platform worker from the frozen gwin0-refresh-source-20261031-a cut (every candidate19-source-20261028-a record byte-identical, plus the Windows inputs checked against 6528ea1) and recomposes the unchanged profile-W composition with the retained PAM helper, runtime archive and model",
    "The cut was captured from the feature/g3-gwin0-beta working tree at b69e093, whose commits after 6528ea1 change only records and documents outside every captured folder; the freeze join and the byte-identical candidate19 records establish that the captured inputs are the 6528ea1 sources",
    "The refresh worker is the workspace release profile (fat LTO, overflow checks, abort on panic, strip) under the owner-approved 8 GiB / 2 CPU / one-job assembly bound. No debug-profile worker was rebuilt; the 2026-10-27 over-cap debug unit stays retained historical evidence and the 64 MiB cap is unchanged"
  ],
